WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.340
Привет!

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.940
Дад-минс-хэллоен-рашен!

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.580
Уэлком-то привет, русский, эпизод 55.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.140
Это 10 июля, 2026 года.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.100
Я, Олья, и today we are going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:12.600
Ready?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:13.360
Поехали!

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.660
Дад-минс, let's go!

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.260
Today's word of the day is samolot.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.600
Са-моя-лёт.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:19.460
Самолёт.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.520
It means airplane.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.000
Imagine a samolot scoring like a silverboard through the sky.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.900
The word even sounds like it is zooming along.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.040
Repeat after me.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.180
Са-моя-лёт.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.140
Now say it fast, самолёт.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.660
Here is a sentence, я лечу на самолёте в Москву.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.340
That means I am flying to Moscow on an airplane.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.580
Now let's build more travel words.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.320
The first one is bilet.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.120
Б-е-лёт, б-лет.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.060
It means ticket.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.120
Repeat after me.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.540
Б-е-лёт, б-лет.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.200
Next comes вокзал.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.720
вокзал, вокзал.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.020
It means train station.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:51.980
Repeat after me.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.320
вокзал, вокзал.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.300
Now that you know bilet, let's add чемодан.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.400
Че модан?

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.420
чемодан?

00:00:58.420 --> 00:00:59.880
It means suitcase.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.100
Repeat after me.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.120
Че модан?

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:02.880
чемодан?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.100
Your чемодан carries your clothes on every trip.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:07.560
Next is passport.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.500
Паспорт.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:09.240
Паспорт.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.520
It means passport.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:11.680
Repeat after me.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:12.420
Паспорт.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.080
Паспорт.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.560
This one looks just like the English word.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.160
Then we have airport.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.720
А-е-ропорт.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:19.880
Аэропорт.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:20.940
It means airport.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.200
Repeat after me.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.560
А-е-ропорт.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:24.320
Аэропорт.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:25.980
Now say the full phrase.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.200
Мы в аэропорту.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.380
Дат means we are at the airport.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.780
Let's keep going with путешествия.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:32.760
Путешествия.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:34.460
Путешествия.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:35.980
It means journey or trip.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.220
Repeat after me.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:38.220
Путешествия.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:40.120
Путешествия.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.240
Your путешествия can take you anywhere.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.380
Next is taxi.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.180
Таксись.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:44.940
Таксись.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:45.840
It means taxi.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:46.920
Repeat after me.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:47.600
Таксись.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:48.360
Таксись.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.820
This word is the same as in English.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.340
Finally we have a tail.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:52.980
Otil.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:53.580
Otil.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:54.480
It means hotel.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.540
Repeat after me.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:56.200
Otil.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:56.740
Otil.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:57.340
Otil.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.540
Рядом с вокзалом means the hotel is near the train station.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.600
Now for a quick grammar bite.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:04.300
The word where means where.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:05.980
It usually starts a question.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.220
Say it with me.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:07.640
Где.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:08.080
Где.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.380
Look at this example.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:10.380
Где вокзал.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.580
It means where is the train station.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.320
Another example is where much mudan.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.060
That means where is my suitcase.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.600
Russian often drops the word is.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.860
So the question feels short and snappy.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.280
In Russia long train journeys are a favorite tradition.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.720
People bring tea in special glasses with metal holders.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.640
They chat for hours as the train rolls along.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.700
The famous Trans-Siberian Railway crosses eight-time zones.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.020
It feels like the ultimate adventure across the country.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.000
Let's practice what we learned.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.980
Do you remember what Somaliot means?

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:44.500
It means airplane.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.560
Try saying bilhet, пожалуйста, when you imagine buying a ticket.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.280
Remember Dome from earlier lessons.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.700
Imagine leaving your Dome, grabbing fruit for the trip

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.760
and asking Zet the platform when boarding poезде.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.860
Draw a big airplane and label it Somaliot if you like to color.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.220
Now hear something really cool about one of today's works.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.540
Want to know a secret about bilhet?

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.220
Did you know that bilhet and the English word ticket

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.600
are actually cousins from the same French route?

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.500
They both come from the old French bilhet,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.420
meaning a short note or document.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.720
This word started in Latin as Bula, a seal or document.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.920
It traveled through French and arrived in Russian in the 1700s

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.720
when Peter the Great opened Russia to European travel.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.860
But be careful, a false friend lurks nearby.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.100
Russian bilhet can also mean an exam ticket or test paper, not just travel.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.320
Next time you buy a ticket, remember it is cousins with bilhet.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.820
They both come from the same Latin seal.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.340
That is your secret short cut to remember him eat forever.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.780
Молодец, that means well done.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.600
Remember every expert started as a beginner.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.160
Practice saying today's words out loud, even just once

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.420
and you'll be amazed how fast you'll learn.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.560
See you next time.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.560
Пока, that's Russian for buy.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.900
And if you'd rather watch them listen, find us on YouTube

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.380
at NERRORU, links in the show notes.

